						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <p>Item #: SCP-5133</p> <p>Object Class: <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Safe</span> Euclid</p> <h2><span>Special Containment Procedures:</span></h2> <p>SCP-5133 Is to be kept in a small glass container. Glass container is to be checked every 4 days for damage. Any personnel entering SCP-5133's chamber are to wear a full hazmat suit and be checked for exposure after exiting the chamber.</p> <h2><span>Description:</span></h2> <p>SCP-5133 is a pale red flower composed of a host's organic tissue. Its' size differs from about 10 to 30 centimetres tall. Analysis of the stem has revealed thousands of tiny hairs that cause an itching sensation upon physical contact.</p> <p>A hole in the center spews a green, fowl smelling gas that irritates the skin wildly.<br /> The purpose of the gas is to spread its' seeds (Designated SCP-5133-A) into its surroundings.<br /> After exiting the flower, the seeds will extend small legs resembling roots to move around. The seeds will then relentlessly try to get to get to the nearest source of living tissue.</p> <p>Once reaching the tissue it will plant itself inside the host, now designated SCP-5133-1. After a period of time that varies from about 40 to 60 minutes that appears to depend on the health of SCP-5133-1, it will start injecting a dangerous toxin inside the host. The toxin's effects include: large rashes, burning sensations inside the body and large growths that burst causing great pain to the host.</p> <p>SCP-5133-A will continue releasing this toxin until SCP-5133-1 is killed. After the host dies, the roots will start making their way deeper into the host's body, consuming small amounts of flesh and bringing them back to the seed. After a suitable amount of flesh is consumed a sapling will form. The flower will take around 5 to 10 days to fully form and then the cycle will repeat.</p> <p>SCP-5133 was discovered in ████,████,Texas on the 13/03/██ by a man who reported a strange<br /> &quot;farting flower&quot; growing out of a dead hedgehog in his yard to the police. The man was later amnesticized and SCP-5133 and SCP-5133-A was contained by the Foundation.</p> <p><strong>Incident Report:</strong> Item: SCP-5133 was reclassified to Euclid after an SCP-5133-A instance was caught on a researcher after she reported a painful sensation on her neck. A full search of the area was conducted and 2 other SCP-5133-A instances were collected and later disposed of correctly.</p> <p><strong>Addendum:</strong> Additional SCP-5133 and SCP-5133-A instances are to be disposed of via incineration. Any SCP-5133-1 instances can be treated with a vaccine created by Dr.████.<br /> SCP-5133-1 instances that have been exposed for over 48 hours cannot be treated and are to be terminated. SCP-5133-A will die off after a day if it does not make contact with living tissue.</p> <p><strong>Addendum 2:</strong> To prevent catastrophic spreading of SCP-5133-A, no more than 3 instances of SCP-5133 are allowed at one time and SCP-5133, SCP-5133-A and SCP-5133-1 is never to enter the outdoors due to threat of containment breach. More SCP-5133 instances are only to be created with the approval of Dr.████.</p> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/clericy" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7190311&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609903495" alt="Clericy" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7190311)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/clericy" >Clericy</a></span></p> 
				 	]]>
